I agree IMO as a caller in `fid` I shouldn't have to worry about this detail.

A possible fix could be to change the `searchable_fields_ids` method to return an enum:

```rust
pub enum SearchableFieldIds {
    UserDefined(Vec<FieldId>),
    Inferred(Vec<FieldId>),
}

impl SearchableFieldIds {
    pub fn into_vec(self) -> Vec<FieldId> { /* ... */ }
}

impl Index {
    pub searchable_fields_ids(&self, txn: &RoTxn<'_>) -> Result<SearchableFieldsIds> { /* ... */ }
}
```

Then my code could become:

```rust
let max_fid = ctx.index.searchable_fields_ids(ctx.txn)?.into_iter().max();
```

while still leaving the possibility for interested callers to match on the enum to know if the searchable fields are inferred or user-defined.

